            "content": "KV cache is an optimization technique in transformer-based language models that stores precomputed key-value pairs from attention computations. During autoregressive generation, each token position produces a key (K) and value (V) tensor through linear projections on the query-key-value (QKV) layers. Rather than recalculating these for every new token against all previous tokens, the model caches K and V tensors after they're computed, avoiding redundant computation during subsequent inference steps."
        },
