            "heading": "How It Works",
            "content": "When generating text token-by-token, the self-attention mechanism requires comparing each new query against all preceding keys to compute attention scores. Without caching, this would mean recomputing the entire key/value projection sequence for every single generated token—O(n×d) operations per step where n is context length and d is hidden dimension size.\n\nKV cache eliminates this redundancy by storing the computed K and V matrices after their initial forward pass. New tokens only need to compute their own Q projection while fetching cached K/V values, reducing per-step complexity significantly and enabling practical inference at longer context lengths."
